      Object {
	$PropName		"MaskObject"
	$ObjectID		47
	$ClassName		"Simulink.Mask"
	Type			"Show_Target"
	Description		"This block returns a VCODE that, when sent to the Process_Video_CMD block, will cause a single target t"
	"o be drawn. Target parameters are specified in the Target Table according to the columns defined below and the row in"
	"put to this block.\n"
	Help			"Used to draw a single, stationary target.\n\n<H2>Library </H2>\nVideo\n\n<H2>Description </H2>\nThis block re"
	"turns a VCODE, which when sent to the Process_Video_CMD block will draw a single stationary target.  The VCODE contai"
	"ns all of the target parameters necessary to draw the target.  \n<P>\nThe VCODE is generated from information contain"
	"ed in the Target Table.  Which parts of the Target Table are used depends on the columns selected (see Parameters and"
	" Dialog Box below)<P>\n\n<p>For example, assume the \"row\" input is 2, the \"type of target\" is set to \"Circle\" a"
	"nd the \"Target Table Columns\" is set to [3 0 0 4]. Then using the sample target table below a red circle will be dr"
	"awn at (20cm, 40cm) and have a radius of 2cm. The zeros in the  \"Target Table Columns\" indicate those parameters ar"
	"e not used.\n\n<tt>\n_____________________________________________<br>\n|&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&n"
	"bsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;| X Pos | Y pos |&nbsp;&nbsp;Fill | Radius |<br>\n---------------------------------------------<br>\n"
	"| target 1 |&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;10 |&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;10 | white |&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;5 |<b"
	"r>\n| target 2 |&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;20 |&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;40 |&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;red |&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbs"
	"p;&nbsp;&nbsp;2 |<br>\n| target 3 |&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-40 |&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;10 |&nbsp;&nbsp;blue |&nbsp;&nbsp;&"
	"nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;3 |<br>\n---------------------------------------------<br>\n</tt>\n<p> Inputs:<br>\n<B> Target"
	"_Row: </B> this scalar input determines which row in the Target Table is used to define the target parameters.  Typic"
	"ally the Target_Row comes from the Trial_Protocol.  <P>\n<B> Target_State: </B> this scalar input determines which st"
	"ate the Target is in.  Different states reference different columns in the Target Table (as defined in the Dialog Box"
	").  Typically the Target_State is controlled by the Stateflow_chart to dynamically change the appearance of the targe"
	"t depending on system and/or subject behavior.  Target_State=0 is a valid input, which turns the target off (the inte"
	"nded method for turning a target off is to set Target_State=0). <BR>\n<P>\nThere is one output from this block: \n<P>"
	"\n<B> VCODE: </B> this output is a vector containing one VCODE.  This output must go to the Process_Video_CMD block o"
	"f the video library for the target to actually be shown (if any other visual targets are to be displayed, then this V"
	"CODE output must be concatenated with the other VCODES prior to connection to the Process_Video_CMD block - see Help "
	"for the Process_Video_CMD block for more information).\n<P>\nTo show multiple targets simultaneously, multiple copies"
	" of the Show_Target block can be used in a Task Program.  The output VCODES from multiple Show_Target blocks must be "
	"concatenated prior to connection to the Process_Video_CMD block.\n<P>\n\n<H2>Parameters and Dialog Box</H2>\n<B>Type "
	"of Target:</B> Choose the type of target specified in the target table. \n<P>\n<B>Number of Target States:</B> Choose"
	" the number of target states specified in each target row.  Up to five target states are allowed per target row.\n<P>"
	"\n<B>State [n] Target Table Columns:</B> Enter the column indices that specify the relevant target attributes in the "
	"Target Table.  All target types have the same first three target attributes: fill colour, stroke colour and stroke wi"
	"dth.\n<Blockquote>\n<P>\nElement 1 (fill colour) - points to the column index in the Target Table containing the fill"
	" colour.  If this index is 0, then the fill colour is transparent and the Target Table is not referenced.  For line t"
	"argets, the fill colour is not used.\n<P>\nElement 2 (stroke colour) - points to the column index in the Target Table"
	" containing the stroke colour.  If this index is 0, then the stroke colour is transparent and the Target Table is not"
	" referenced.  It is possible to use the same column index for both fill colour and stroke colour (i.e.  if single-col"
	"our targets are desired).  For line targets, stroke colour defines the colour of the line.\n<P>\nElement 3 (stroke wi"
	"dth) - points to the column index in the Target Table containing the stroke width (cm).  If no stroke is desired, the"
	"n setting the stroke column index to 0 will produce a stroke width of 0  and the Target Table is not referenced.  Set"
	"ting stroke column index to a value less than;0 will produce a standard 1 mm stroke width, again without referencing "
	"the Target Table.  For line targets, stroke width defines the width of the line.\n<P>\n<B><I>Circle</I></B> <P>\nElem"
	"ent 4 (radius) - radius of the circle (cm).\n<P>\n<B><I>Ellipse</I></B> <P>\nElements 4-6 (ellipse properties) - majo"
	"r radius (cm), minor radius (cm), rotation angle (degrees).  If no rotation is desired, then setting rotation column "
	"index to 0 will produce a default rotation of 0 and the Target Table will not be referenced.\n<P>\n<B><I>Rectangle</I"
	"></B><P>\nElements 4-6 (rectangle properties) - length (cm), height (cm), rotation angle (degrees).  If no rotation i"
	"s desired, then setting rotation column index to 0 will produce a default rotation of 0 and the Target Table will not"
	" be referenced.\n<P>\n<B><I>Line</I></B><P>\nElements 4-5 (line properties) - end point x-axis position relative to s"
	"tart point (cm), end point y-axis position relative to start point (cm). The width and colour of the line are defined"
	" by the stroke width and the stroke colour, respectively.  The fill colour column is ignored (i.e. any value can be u"
	"sed for column 1)\n<P>\n<B><I>Triangle</I></B><P>\nElements 4-7 (triangle properties) - length (cm), height (cm), off"
	"set of peak of triangle relative to midpoint of the length (cm), rotation angle (degrees). If a height column index o"
	"f 0 is specified, then an equilateral triangle with sides of the specified length will be created and the Target Tabl"
	"e will not be referenced for height or peak offset.  If no rotation is desired, then setting a rotation column index "
	"of 0 will produce a default rotation of 0 and the Target Table will not be referenced.\n</Blockquote>\n<P>\nEach targ"
	"et state requires its own set of column index definitions (although multiple states can point to the same column inde"
	"x if desired).<P>\n<H2>Examples</H2>\n<B>Example 1.</B>  Suppose a target row will be used to define 2 states for a c"
	"ircle type target.  The first state will be a solid circle of colour1 and the second state will be identical, except "
	"that it will have colour2.  The related Target Table columns are: column 4 = colour1; column 5 = colour2 and column 6"
	" = radius.  For this example, \"State 1 Target Table Columns\" would equal [4 4 0 6], while \"State 2 Target Table Co"
	"lumns\" would equal [5 5 0 6].  In other words, the fill and stroke colours are both taken from the same column of th"
	"e Target Table, and there is no outside stroke.\n<P> \n\n<B>Example 2.</B>  Suppose a target row will be used to defi"
	"ne 2 states for an circle type target.  The first state will have fill colour \"colour1\" and stroke colour \"colour2"
	"\" and radius \"rad1\".  The second state will have fill colour \"colour3\" and stroke colour \"colour2\" and radius "
	"\"rad2\".  Both states will have stroke width \"str_width\".  The related Target Table columns are: column4 = colour1"
	"; column 5 = colour2; column 6 = colour3; column 7 = str_width; column 8 = rad1; column 9 = rad2.  For this example, "
	"\"State 1 Target Table Columns\" would equal [4 5 7 8], while \"State 2 Target Table Columns\" would equal [6 5 7 9]."
	"  \n<P>\n\n<B>Example 3.</B>  Suppose a target row will be used to define 1 state for an ellipse type target.  It wil"
	"l be an outline ellipse with a stroke colour but no fill colour and a standard 1mm stroke width.  The related Target "
	"Table columns are: column 4 = colour; column 5 = major radius; column 6 = minor radius and column 7 = orientation.  F"
	"or this example, \"State 1 Target Table Columns\" would equal [0 4 -1 5 6 7].\n<P> \n\n<H2>Related Blocks </H2>\nShow"
	"_Target_With_Label<BR>\nProcess_Video_CMD"
	Initialization		"block_path = gcb;  % store block path, as gcb may change with block operations\n\n% Handle backgroun"
	"d colours if link status changes.  If the link is resolved, \n% make the block back to the library colour.  If the li"
	"nk is not resolved, \n% change the colour to something other than the library block colour (but \n% only change it if"
	" it is the library colour, that way end-users can choose\n% their own colour.\nlink_status = get_param(block_path, 'L"
	"inkStatus');\nblock_parent = get_param(block_path, 'Parent');\nif strcmp(link_status, 'resolved') || strcmp(block_par"
	"ent, 'Video')\n	set_param(block_path, 'BackgroundColor', '[0.85882, 0.69019, 0.3098]');\nelse\n 	current_bgcolor = st"
	"r2num( get_param(block_path, 'BackgroundColor') ) ;\n	%if the BackgroundColor is 'green', then after the str2num, cur"
	"rent_bgcolor is empty\n	if ~isempty(current_bgcolor) \n		if (round(current_bgcolor * 255) == [219 176 79])\n	 		set_p"
	"aram(block_path, 'BackgroundColor', 'green');\n		end\n	end\nend\n\nnum_states=str2num(get_param(gcb, 'num_states'));\n"
	"columntext='';\n\nfor i=1:num_states\n	varname=['attribcol' num2str(i)];\n	if i>1\n		columntext=strvcat(columntext, g"
	"et_param(gcb, varname));\n	else\n		columntext=[get_param(gcb, varname)];\n	end\nend\n\nspace=[''];\nn=round(length(co"
	"lumntext)/2)-4;\nfor i=1:n\n	space=[space ' '];\nend\ncolumntext=strvcat([space '(columns)'], columntext);\n\noutput_"
	"block=char(find_system(gcb,'LookUnderMasks','all','FollowLinks','on','SearchDepth',1,'BlockType','Outport'));\noutput"
	"name=get_param(output_block,'Name');\ninput_block=find_system(gcb,'LookUnderMasks','all','FollowLinks','on','SearchDe"
	"pth',1,'BlockType','Inport');\ninputname1=get_param(char(input_block{1}),'Name');\ninputname2=get_param(char(input_bl"
	"ock{2}),'Name');\n\nif length(input_block) >= 3\n    inputname3=get_param(char(input_block{3}),'Name');\nend\n\nsourc"
	"e=get_param(gcb,'source');\nvis=get_param(gcb,'MaskVisibilities');\nnum_states=str2num(get_param(gcb, 'num_states'));"
	"\n\nif source=='internal'\n	if length(input_block) == 3\n		pos=get_param([gcb '/Opacity'],'position');\n		delete_line"
	"(gcb, 'Opacity/1', 'Embedded MATLAB Function/4');\n		delete_block(input_block{3});\n        add_block('built-in/Const"
	"ant',[gcb '/Opacity'],'Name','Opacity');\n		set_param([gcb '/Opacity'],'position',pos);\n		add_line(gcb, 'Opacity/1',"
	" 'Embedded MATLAB Function/4');\n		set_param([gcb '/Opacity'],'Value','opacity');\n	end\n	displaytext = ['disp(column"
	"text); port_label(''output'',1,outputname); port_label(''input'',1, inputname1); port_label(''input'',2, inputname2);"
	"'];\n	vis{10}='on';\nelse\n	if length(input_block) == 2\n		pos=get_param([gcb '/Opacity'],'position');\n		delete_line"
	"(gcb, 'Opacity/1', 'Embedded MATLAB Function/4');\n		delete_block([gcb, '/Opacity']);\n		add_block('built-in/Inport',"
	"[gcb '/In2'],'Name','Opacity');\n		set_param([gcb '/Opacity'],'position',pos);\n		add_line(gcb, 'Opacity/1', 'Embedde"
	"d MATLAB Function/4');\n 	end\n	inputname3='Opacity';\n	displaytext = ['disp(columntext); port_label(''output'',1,out"
	"putname); port_label(''input'',1, inputname1); port_label(''input'',2, inputname2); port_label(''input'',3, inputname"
	"3);'];\n	vis{10}='off';\nend\n\ntargetDisplay = get_param(gcb,'target_display');\n\nif length(targetDisplay) == lengt"
	"h('Subject display only')\n    set_param([gcb '/Target_Display'], 'Value', '2');\nelseif length(targetDisplay) == len"
	"gth('Operator display only')\n    set_param([gcb '/Target_Display'], 'Value', '3');\nelse\n    set_param([gcb '/Targe"
	"t_Display'], 'Value', '1');\nend\n    \nset_param(gcb,'MaskVisibilities',vis);\nset_param(gcb,'MaskDisplay',displayte"
	"xt);\n"
	SelfModifiable		"on"
	Display			"disp(columntext); port_label('output',1,outputname); port_label('input',1, inputname1); port_label('input'"
	",2, inputname2);"
	IconUnits		"normalized"
	Array {
	  Type			  "Simulink.MaskParameter"
	  Dimension		  11
	  Object {
	    $ObjectID		    48
	    Type		    "popup"
	    Array {
	      Type		      "Cell"
	      Dimension		      5
	      Cell		      "Circle"
	      Cell		      "Ellipse"
	      Cell		      "Rectangle"
	      Cell		      "Line"
	      Cell		      "Triangle"
	      PropName		      "TypeOptions"
	    }
	    Name		    "target_type"
	    Prompt		    "Type of Target"
	    Value		    "Circle"
	    Callback		    "target_type=get_param(gcb, 'target_type');\nattribcol1=[str2num(get_param(gcb, 'attribcol1')) 0 0 "
	    "0 0 0 0];\nattribcol2=[str2num(get_param(gcb, 'attribcol2')) 0 0 0 0 0 0];\nattribcol3=[str2num(get_param(gcb, 'a"
	    "ttribcol3')) 0 0 0 0 0 0];\nattribcol4=[str2num(get_param(gcb, 'attribcol4')) 0 0 0 0 0 0];\nattribcol5=[str2num("
	    "get_param(gcb, 'attribcol5')) 0 0 0 0 0 0];\nswitch target_type(1:3)\n	case 'Cir'\n		numcol=4;\n	case 'Ell'\n		nu"
	    "mcol=6;\n    case 'Rec'\n        numcol=6;\n    case 'Lin'\n        numcol=5;\n    case 'Tri'\n        numcol=7;\n"
	    "    otherwise\n		numcol=4;\nend\nset_param(gcb, 'attribcol1', mat2str(attribcol1(1:numcol)));\nset_param(gcb, 'at"
	    "tribcol2', mat2str(attribcol2(1:numcol)));\nset_param(gcb, 'attribcol3', mat2str(attribcol3(1:numcol)));\nset_par"
	    "am(gcb, 'attribcol4', mat2str(attribcol4(1:numcol)));\nset_param(gcb, 'attribcol5', mat2str(attribcol5(1:numcol))"
	    ");\n\nstateindices_padding=zeros(5,7);\nset_param(gcb, 'stateindices_padding', mat2str(stateindices_padding(:, 1:"
	    "(11-numcol))));"
	  }
	  Object {
	    $ObjectID		    49
	    Type		    "popup"
	    Array {
	      Type		      "Cell"
	      Dimension		      5
	      Cell		      "1"
	      Cell		      "2"
	      Cell		      "3"
	      Cell		      "4"
	      Cell		      "5"
	      PropName		      "TypeOptions"
	    }
	    Name		    "num_states"
	    Prompt		    "Number of Target States"
	    Value		    "1"
	    Callback		    "main_block=gcb;\nnum_states=str2num(get_param(main_block, 'num_states'));\nvis=get_param(main_bloc"
	    "k,'MaskVisibilities');\n\n%If the number of states>1, then output an array instead of a vector.\n%Only show those"
	    " inputs necessary on the Mask\noutput_block=char(find_system(gcb,'LookUnderMasks','all','SearchDepth',1,'BlockTyp"
	    "e','Outport'));\nif num_states==1			%output of HandInTarget block is a vector\n	vis{4}='off';\n	vis{5}='off';\n	v"
	    "is{6}='off';\n	vis{7}='off';\nelseif num_states==2					%output of HandInTarget block is an array\n	vis{4}='on';\n"
	    "	vis{5}='off';\n	vis{6}='off';\n	vis{7}='off';\nelseif num_states==3					%output of HandInTarget block is an arra"
	    "y\n	vis{4}='on';\n	vis{5}='on';\n	vis{6}='off';\n	vis{7}='off';\nelseif num_states==4					%output of HandInTarget"
	    " block is an array\n	vis{4}='on';\n	vis{5}='on';\n	vis{6}='on';\n	vis{7}='off';\nelse								%output of HandInTar"
	    "get block is an array\n	vis{4}='on';\n	vis{5}='on';\n	vis{6}='on';\n	vis{7}='on';\nend\nset_param(main_block,'Mas"
	    "kVisibilities',vis);\n\ntarget_type=get_param(gcb, 'target_type');\nattribcol1=[str2num(get_param(gcb, 'attribcol"
	    "1')) 0 0 0 0 0 0];\nattribcol2=[str2num(get_param(gcb, 'attribcol2')) 0 0 0 0 0 0];\nattribcol3=[str2num(get_para"
	    "m(gcb, 'attribcol3')) 0 0 0 0 0 0];\nattribcol4=[str2num(get_param(gcb, 'attribcol4')) 0 0 0 0 0 0];\nattribcol5="
	    "[str2num(get_param(gcb, 'attribcol5')) 0 0 0 0 0 0];\nswitch target_type(1:3)\n	case 'Cir'\n		numcol=4;\n	case 'E"
	    "ll'\n		numcol=6;\n    case 'Rec'\n        numcol=6;\n    case 'Lin'\n        numcol=5;\n    case 'Tri'\n        n"
	    "umcol=7;\n    otherwise\n		numcol=4;\nend\nset_param(gcb, 'attribcol1', mat2str(attribcol1(1:numcol)));\nset_para"
	    "m(gcb, 'attribcol2', mat2str(attribcol2(1:numcol)));\nset_param(gcb, 'attribcol3', mat2str(attribcol3(1:numcol)))"
	    ";\nset_param(gcb, 'attribcol4', mat2str(attribcol4(1:numcol)));\nset_param(gcb, 'attribcol5', mat2str(attribcol5("
	    "1:numcol)));\n\nstateindices_padding=zeros(5,7);\nset_param(gcb, 'stateindices_padding', mat2str(stateindices_pad"
	    "ding(:, 1:(11-numcol))));"
	  }
	  Object {
	    $ObjectID		    50
	    Type		    "edit"
	    Name		    "attribcol1"
	    Prompt		    "State 1 Target Table Column(s)"
	    Value		    "[6 6 0 3]"
	    Callback		    "target_type=get_param(gcb, 'target_type');\nattribcol1=[str2num(get_param(gcb, 'attribcol1')) 0 0 "
	    "0 0 0 0];\nattribcol2=[str2num(get_param(gcb, 'attribcol2')) 0 0 0 0 0 0];\nattribcol3=[str2num(get_param(gcb, 'a"
	    "ttribcol3')) 0 0 0 0 0 0];\nattribcol4=[str2num(get_param(gcb, 'attribcol4')) 0 0 0 0 0 0];\nattribcol5=[str2num("
	    "get_param(gcb, 'attribcol5')) 0 0 0 0 0 0];\nswitch target_type(1:3)\n	case 'Cir'\n		numcol=4;\n	case 'Ell'\n		nu"
	    "mcol=6;\n    case 'Rec'\n        numcol=6;\n    case 'Lin'\n        numcol=5;\n    case 'Tri'\n        numcol=7;\n"
	    "    otherwise\n		numcol=4;\nend\nset_param(gcb, 'attribcol1', mat2str(attribcol1(1:numcol)));\nset_param(gcb, 'at"
	    "tribcol2', mat2str(attribcol2(1:numcol)));\nset_param(gcb, 'attribcol3', mat2str(attribcol3(1:numcol)));\nset_par"
	    "am(gcb, 'attribcol4', mat2str(attribcol4(1:numcol)));\nset_param(gcb, 'attribcol5', mat2str(attribcol5(1:numcol))"
	    ");\n\nstateindices_padding=zeros(5,7);\nset_param(gcb, 'stateindices_padding', mat2str(stateindices_padding(:, 1:"
	    "(11-numcol))));"
	  }
	  Object {
	    $ObjectID		    51
	    Type		    "edit"
	    Name		    "attribcol2"
	    Prompt		    "State 2 Target Table Column(s)"
	    Value		    "[6 6 0 3]"
	    Visible		    "off"
	    Callback		    "target_type=get_param(gcb, 'target_type');\nattribcol1=[str2num(get_param(gcb, 'attribcol1')) 0 0 "
	    "0 0 0 0];\nattribcol2=[str2num(get_param(gcb, 'attribcol2')) 0 0 0 0 0 0];\nattribcol3=[str2num(get_param(gcb, 'a"
	    "ttribcol3')) 0 0 0 0 0 0];\nattribcol4=[str2num(get_param(gcb, 'attribcol4')) 0 0 0 0 0 0];\nattribcol5=[str2num("
	    "get_param(gcb, 'attribcol5')) 0 0 0 0 0 0];\nswitch target_type(1:3)\n	case 'Cir'\n		numcol=4;\n	case 'Ell'\n		nu"
	    "mcol=6;\n    case 'Rec'\n        numcol=6;\n    case 'Lin'\n        numcol=5;\n    case 'Tri'\n        numcol=7;\n"
	    "    otherwise\n		numcol=4;\nend\nset_param(gcb, 'attribcol1', mat2str(attribcol1(1:numcol)));\nset_param(gcb, 'at"
	    "tribcol2', mat2str(attribcol2(1:numcol)));\nset_param(gcb, 'attribcol3', mat2str(attribcol3(1:numcol)));\nset_par"
	    "am(gcb, 'attribcol4', mat2str(attribcol4(1:numcol)));\nset_param(gcb, 'attribcol5', mat2str(attribcol5(1:numcol))"
	    ");\n\nstateindices_padding=zeros(5,7);\nset_param(gcb, 'stateindices_padding', mat2str(stateindices_padding(:, 1:"
	    "(11-numcol))));"
	  }
	  Object {
	    $ObjectID		    52
	    Type		    "edit"
	    Name		    "attribcol3"
	    Prompt		    "State 3 Target Table Column(s)"
	    Value		    "[7 7 0 3]"
	    Visible		    "off"
	    Callback		    "target_type=get_param(gcb, 'target_type');\nattribcol1=[str2num(get_param(gcb, 'attribcol1')) 0 0 "
	    "0 0 0 0];\nattribcol2=[str2num(get_param(gcb, 'attribcol2')) 0 0 0 0 0 0];\nattribcol3=[str2num(get_param(gcb, 'a"
	    "ttribcol3')) 0 0 0 0 0 0];\nattribcol4=[str2num(get_param(gcb, 'attribcol4')) 0 0 0 0 0 0];\nattribcol5=[str2num("
	    "get_param(gcb, 'attribcol5')) 0 0 0 0 0 0];\nswitch target_type(1:3)\n	case 'Cir'\n		numcol=4;\n	case 'Ell'\n		nu"
	    "mcol=6;\n    case 'Rec'\n        numcol=6;\n    case 'Lin'\n        numcol=5;\n    case 'Tri'\n        numcol=7;\n"
	    "    otherwise\n		numcol=4;\nend\nset_param(gcb, 'attribcol1', mat2str(attribcol1(1:numcol)));\nset_param(gcb, 'at"
	    "tribcol2', mat2str(attribcol2(1:numcol)));\nset_param(gcb, 'attribcol3', mat2str(attribcol3(1:numcol)));\nset_par"
	    "am(gcb, 'attribcol4', mat2str(attribcol4(1:numcol)));\nset_param(gcb, 'attribcol5', mat2str(attribcol5(1:numcol))"
	    ");\n\nstateindices_padding=zeros(5,7);\nset_param(gcb, 'stateindices_padding', mat2str(stateindices_padding(:, 1:"
	    "(11-numcol))));"
	  }
	  Object {
	    $ObjectID		    53
	    Type		    "edit"
	    Name		    "attribcol4"
	    Prompt		    "State 4 Target Table Column(s)"
	    Value		    "[8 8 0 3]"
	    Visible		    "off"
	    Callback		    "target_type=get_param(gcb, 'target_type');\nattribcol1=[str2num(get_param(gcb, 'attribcol1')) 0 0 "
	    "0 0 0 0];\nattribcol2=[str2num(get_param(gcb, 'attribcol2')) 0 0 0 0 0 0];\nattribcol3=[str2num(get_param(gcb, 'a"
	    "ttribcol3')) 0 0 0 0 0 0];\nattribcol4=[str2num(get_param(gcb, 'attribcol4')) 0 0 0 0 0 0];\nattribcol5=[str2num("
	    "get_param(gcb, 'attribcol5')) 0 0 0 0 0 0];\nswitch target_type(1:3)\n	case 'Cir'\n		numcol=4;\n	case 'Ell'\n		nu"
	    "mcol=6;\n    case 'Rec'\n        numcol=6;\n    case 'Lin'\n        numcol=5;\n    case 'Tri'\n        numcol=7;\n"
	    "    otherwise\n		numcol=4;\nend\nset_param(gcb, 'attribcol1', mat2str(attribcol1(1:numcol)));\nset_param(gcb, 'at"
	    "tribcol2', mat2str(attribcol2(1:numcol)));\nset_param(gcb, 'attribcol3', mat2str(attribcol3(1:numcol)));\nset_par"
	    "am(gcb, 'attribcol4', mat2str(attribcol4(1:numcol)));\nset_param(gcb, 'attribcol5', mat2str(attribcol5(1:numcol))"
	    ");\n\nstateindices_padding=zeros(5,7);\nset_param(gcb, 'stateindices_padding', mat2str(stateindices_padding(:, 1:"
	    "(11-numcol))));"
	  }
